  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows actors to modify tasks in teams they are not members of, directly violating the cross-team isolation invariant (FR-014). The assertion checks that every audit entry's actor is a member of the task's team.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_014_CrossTeamIsolation
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_014_CrossTeamIsolation: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows non-owner members to edit or delete tasks they do not own, and allows non-admin members to modify tasks at all. This directly violates FR-008/009/010.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, LeastPrivilege
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_TaskHasCreatedAuditEntry  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_TaskHasCreatedAuditEntry.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows tasks to exist without a 'created' audit entry, violating FR-015 which requires every task to have an audit trail starting with creation.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_PerEditEventAudit
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_PerEditEventAudit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ActorRoleSnapshot  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_ActorRoleSnapshot.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows audit entries to record an actor's role that differs from their actual role in that team at the time of the change, violating FR-015's requirement for role snapshots.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing this fact removes the definition of which roles can perform which operations, allowing the model to explore inconsistent permission states and violating the feature's permission matrix contract.
    expected to FAIL: PermissionCompleteness, LeastPrivilege
      - PermissionCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)

